# The main scenario: a typical game, from orbit to an Ark leaving a developed planet.
#
# `spec/scenarios.md`: there is one main scenario and it touches everything a typical game
# uses. It is the foundation, and it is vetted by hand. A mechanic that only appears in an
# unusual situation belongs in a scenario of its own - so nothing here starves and nothing
# is lost to nature, and both get scenarios of their own once this one satisfies its reader.
#
# Every line is a command. There is no other way for the state to move, so this file is a
# complete account of how the game got where `scenario/expected/play.4x` says it is.
#
# **Storage is the constraint now** - `S-44`. A territory declares **no limit** for a
# resource; it holds what its stores hold, and a store holds ten. An extractor holds
# nothing, so what is produced goes into a store, is spent the turn it is made, or is lost
# when that turn ends. A founding leaves a food store and a metal store and no energy store,
# which is why energy is the resource this game has to build for.

# Turn 1. The Ark lands on territory 1 and becomes the ground: a garrison, two citizens, a
# farm, a mine, and somewhere to put what each of them digs.
{deploy-ark territory:1}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:metal}
{end-turn}

# Turn 2. Four citizens. The farm makes four and the store holds ten, so the second farm can
# wait; the mine pays for a second store first, because metal with nowhere to go is lost.
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:1}
{build-extractor territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{build-store territory:1 resource:food}
{end-turn}

# Turn 3. Two farms, and four citizens - so four labor, and four things this turn can do.
# The second mine waits a turn for the population to pay for it.
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:1}
{build-store territory:1 resource:metal}
{end-turn}

# Turn 4. The last farm and the first well. Energy has nowhere to go until it has a store,
# which is the shape `S-44` gave the middle of this game.
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:1}
{build-extractor territory:1 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:1}
{build-extractor territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{build-extractor territory:1 resource:energy}
{create-labor territory:1}
{build-store territory:1 resource:energy}
{end-turn}

# Turn 5. Everything the ground has room for is built, bar the last mine and the last wells.
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:energy}
{create-labor territory:1}
{build-extractor territory:1 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:1}
{build-extractor territory:1 resource:energy}
{end-turn}

# Turn 6. Twelve of each a turn, and a pioneer costs three metal and six energy.
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:energy}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:energy}
{create-labor territory:1}
{build-extractor territory:1 resource:energy}
{create-labor territory:1}
{build-store territory:1 resource:energy}
{end-turn}

# Turn 7. The pioneer, and the last stores this territory will need.
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:energy}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:energy}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:energy}
{create-labor territory:1}
{build-store territory:1 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:1}
{produce-pioneer territory:1}
{end-turn}

# Turn 8. The pioneer crosses into territory 2. It does not become it: `S-76`, founding
# requires the pioneer to be standing on the ground, so crossing and founding are two acts a
# turn apart. `P-214` still holds - the player says which recipe this is, and moving onto
# unclaimed ground founds nothing.
{move unit:pioneer from:1 to:2}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:energy}
{create-labor territory:1}
{build-yard territory:1}
{end-turn}

# Turn 9. The pioneer founds the ground it crossed to, and the Ark follows: three metal and
# twelve energy against a Yard. The new ground feeds itself from the turn it is claimed.
{found-by-land territory:2}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:energy}
{create-labor territory:1}
{launch-ark territory:1}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:food}

{end-turn}

# Turn 10. No Ark crosses, and the reason is not the one written here until `S-165`.
#
# **The comment said launching puts nothing into orbit and that was false.** `P-342` made
# launching one recipe that pays an Ark's cost at a Yard, and that recipe has always carried a
# `produce 1 ark above $where` row - the model fired four of its five. Sean settled it in
# `P-549`: *yes launching leaves the ark in orbit, we spend materials from the surface and end
# up with an ark in orbit, and an ark is never on the surface.*
#
# **So there is an Ark, and it does not cross because nothing here tells it to.** An Ark moves
# in orbit and lands by `deploy-ark`; this scenario launches one on turn 10 and stops, so the
# state it leaves has an Ark above territory 1. **What is untested is orbital movement**, which
# is a gap in the scenario rather than a fact about the rules - and it was reported as one for
# three days because a comment explained the absence. The pioneer's crossing on turn 8 is
# the move this file fires, and it fires because founding needs it rather than because a case
# was written to exercise it - `C-63` answered by `S-76`.
# The farms are worked first, as always: a population that gathers nothing this turn starves
# at the end of it, whatever else is going on.
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:food}

# **And the Ark that turn 9 launched mines from the sun** - `P-552`, which is what gives an orbit
# anything in it. `spec/units.md`: *a mobile unit that moves in orbit gathers its own energy from
# the sun. It mines one unit.*
#
# **One unit is exactly one crossing**, which is the Ark's `Fuel` of 1 - so this is the state a
# reader needs to see the loop at all: an orbit with something in it, and a unit that could spend
# it. **Nothing crosses yet**, because a second orbit to cross to is the scenario's next gap and
# not this recipe's.
#
# **It survives the turn's end**, and that is the tank doing the one thing a tank does: an orbit
# declares no room of its own, so what is mined is kept only while the Ark that mined it is still
# there to hold it.
{mine-energy territory:1}
{end-turn}

# Turn 11. The second territory starts building, and `R-6` is why. **Its *vetted when* asks for
# an Ark launched from the second territory**, so everything from here is territory 2 paying for
# a Yard out of ground that is poorer than the landing site's: two metal at density four, two
# energy at density four, and **no stores at all, because `P-427` took them out of founding.**
#
# **So the first metal it digs buys somewhere to put the next.** A store is what makes a turn's
# production survive the turn, and a Yard costs fifteen metal - which is four turns of this
# ground even with both mines running, and impossible in any number of turns without a store.
#
# Territory 1 does exactly what it did on turn 10: eight citizens, two farms worked, eight food
# against eight upkeep. **It is stable rather than idle** - a population that gathers nothing
# starves, and this one gathers precisely what it eats.
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:2}
{build-store territory:2 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:2}
{build-extractor territory:2 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:2}
{build-extractor territory:2 resource:energy}
{end-turn}

# Turn 12. The second metal store, which the second mine has just licensed - a store is bounded
# by the extractors of its resource, so two mines is what makes two stores legal, and twenty
# metal is what makes fifteen reachable at all.
#
# **And the first energy store.** Energy is the resource this ground has to build for twice over:
# a Yard needs metal and the Ark it produces needs twelve energy, which is more than one store
# holds.
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:2}
{build-store territory:2 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:2}
{build-extractor territory:2 resource:energy}
{create-labor territory:2}
{build-store territory:2 resource:energy}
{end-turn}

# Turn 13. Everything territory 2 will ever build is built after this turn, and the two wells
# start running. Twelve energy needs two stores and two turns of both wells.
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:2}
{build-store territory:2 resource:energy}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:energy}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:energy}
{end-turn}

# Turn 14. The Yard, for fifteen of the seventeen metal this ground has saved - and the mines
# and wells keep running behind it, because the Ark still wants three metal and twelve energy.
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:2}
{build-yard territory:2}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:metal}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:energy}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:energy}
{end-turn}

# Turn 15. **The Ark leaves the second territory, which is what `R-6` is checked against**: the
# scenario took its first territory from orbit, its second by land, and launches from the second.
#
# **Two citizens go with it**, which is the cost the recipe states and the reason this territory
# ends the game at six rather than eight - the food it grows pays for two more before the turn is
# over. **There is now an Ark above each of the two territories the player holds**, one launched
# from the landing site on turn 9 and one from the ground that had to build for it.
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:1}
{work territory:1 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:2}
{work territory:2 resource:food}
{create-labor territory:2}
{launch-ark territory:2}
{end-turn}
